                <pb facs="1665" n="1641" sameAs="frus:frus1950v03/pg1641"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>The Foreign Ministers of the United States, the United Kingdom, and France met in
                    London May 11–13 to discuss world problems of mutual concern. Concurrent with
                    the ministerial talks were various bilateral and trilateral discussions on
                    problems that the Ministers did not have time to consider. In particular
                    American and British officials held six bilateral discussions on various aspects
                    of Anglo-American relations. For documentation on these bilateral talks and the
                    meetings of the Ministers, see pages 828 ff.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
